{#
Generated by: Claude Code CLI
Date time: 2026/09/09 03:10 SAST
Version: 0.7
Description:
  The Help Centre.

  Grouped accordions, two levels deep. The flat list this replaced had eight topics at one level,
  which is a menu rather than a structure: a reader who wanted to know how course credits work had
  to read every summary to find out that the answer was not there.

  Two levels is the limit. A third would be a table of contents pretending to be a page, and the
  answers here are short enough that finding one should never take three clicks.

  Every group is closed except the first. A page that opens everything is a long document with
  headings, which is what accordions exist to avoid; a page that opens nothing makes the reader
  work to see that there is anything here at all.

  The disclosure elements are details and summary, so the page works with no JavaScript, is
  keyboard-navigable by the browser rather than by us, and is searchable with the browser's own
  find because an open group stays open.

Changelog:
  2026/09/09 03:10 SAST
  - Rebuilt as grouped accordions with sub-accordions, and brought the theme topics up to Theme
    Package 4.0.
  2026/09/07 15:00 SAST
